Tool Purpose <code>create_upload_url()</code> Single-use upload link, valid 10 minutes, for one file up to the hub limit (200 MiB) → <code>{upload_url, token_header, token, expires_at, max_bytes, curl}</code>. The agent runs <code>curl</code> in its shell with the file path filled in and gets <code>{upload_id, sha256, size}</code>. The file's bytes go straight to the hub and never pass through the model. <code>upload_content(filename, content_base64, sha256)</code> Upload a tiny file inline (at most 8 MiB decoded) → <code>{upload_id, sha256, size}</code>. <code>sha256</code> is the hex digest of the original file; if the decoded content does not match it, nothing is uploaded. Models copy long base64 strings unreliably, so prefer <code>create_upload_url</code> for anything but a few KB. <code>transcribe_audio(upload_id \| path, execution_profile?, language?, profile?, options?, private=true, idempotency_key?)</code> Submit an audio job → <code>{job_id, status, private}</code> immediately. <code>options</code>: <code>translate</code>, <code>word_timestamps</code>, <code>vad_filter</code>. <code>convert_document(upload_id \| path, …, options?)</code> Submit a PDF/image → Markdown job → <code>{job_id, status, private}</code>. <code>options</code>: <code>languages</code> (<code>de</code>, <code>en</code>, <code>fr</code>, <code>it</code>, <code>es</code>, <code>ko</code>), <code>ocr</code>, <code>ocr_engine</code>, <code>page_start</code>, <code>page_end</code>, <code>pipeline</code>, <code>image_scale</code> (1.0–4.0, OCR raster multiplier), <code>ocr_min_confidence</code> (0–1, <code>rapidocr</code> only); see the API reference. <code>get_job(job_id)</code> Status (<code>pending</code> with <code>queue_reason</code>, <code>processing</code>, <code>completed</code>, <code>failed</code>, <code>cancelled</code>). <code>get_result(job_id, offset=0, limit=32768)</code> One Markdown chunk plus <code>next_offset</code>, <code>total_chars</code>, language, warnings, provenance. Each call is one hub range read (<code>GET /v1/jobs/{id}/result/markdown</code>), so the full result never passes through the MCP server. Concatenating chunks from offset 0 until <code>next_offset</code> is <code>null</code> reproduces the REST <code>markdown</code> exactly. <code>limit</code> is capped at 32 768 characters. <code>cancel_job(job_id)</code> Request cancellation; later worker output is rejected. <code>list_engines()</code> The organization's execution profiles (approved engine/model/accelerator candidates) and the engines it can use now (<code>GET /v1/engines</code>: tuples that an approved worker of the organization has tested; cloud providers only when cloud processing is enabled). <code>get_settings()</code> The organization's current non-secret settings revision (read-only). <p>There are no tools that change settings or profiles, issue or revoke credentials, or enroll workers. Use <code>resona settings</code> and <code>resona-admin</code> for those.</p> <p>Jobs are private by default. <code>private=false</code> only works when the organization has enabled cloud processing; otherwise the hub answers <code>policy_denied</code>. There is no fallback to another provider or to local processing.</p> <p>A typical agent flow:</p> <pre><code>create_upload_url()                            → {curl: "curl … -F 'file=@&lt;PATH&gt;' …"}
$ curl … -F 'file=@memo.wav' …                 → {upload_id}
transcribe_audio(upload_id=…)                  → {job_id: 12, status: "pending", private: true}
get_job(12)                                    → … status: "completed"
get_result(12)                                 → {markdown: "...", next_offset: 32768, total_chars: 51234}
get_result(12, offset=32768)                   → … until next_offset is null
</code></pre>
